			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "34d7b7e653beb57258759d4db49af58c4fda4e73"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T15:34:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element and Dependency submodules and migrate to pnpm v11\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit 40a70b7 to integrate the latest architectural refinements and build pipeline updates across the Mountain native backend, Wind service layer, and Cocoon extension host. Key changes include localizing the `call!` macro for strict closure hygiene, enhancing the `proxy_cocoon` utility for error mapping, and ensuring immediate `$acceptModelSaved` notifications to Cocoon for Sky-initiated saves. Additionally, refresh Wind's codegen pipeline to align TypeScript contracts with upstream VS Code changes and expand Output IPC stubs for UI channels.\n\nUpdate the Dependency (VS Code) submodule to commit ed34d13 to incorporate upstream stability fixes and security hardening, including the Agent Host refactor, MCP OAuth secret storage in OS secure vaults, and path traversal rejection.\n\nMigrate the project package manager to pnpm v11.2.2 by removing the `pnpm` configuration block from `package.json` and explicitly moving `onlyBuiltDependencies`, `linkWorkspacePackages`, and build allow-lists to `pnpm-workspace.yaml` to align with the new schema and improve workspace resolution.",
			"SHA": "8f4011d9458b8afd79976351943ebfa17993a433"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T11:13:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to centralize Cocoon IPC and URI sanitization\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 31f4058 to 6b92b99 to continue standardizing the Mountain native backend IPC layer.\n\n**Mountain:** Introduce the `proxy_cocoon` helper in `Utilities::Proxy` to abstract `ApplicationRunTime` retrieval and method string construction, replacing verbose inline `SendRequestToSideCar` logic across `CustomEditorProvider`, `StatusBarProvider`, `TestProvider`, `Authentication`, `Task`, and `FileSystem` handlers. Additionally, centralize URI sanitization by extracting `StripFileUriScheme` into `Utilities::Params` as `strip_file_uri`, applying it to all `FileSystem` operations to consistently normalize `file://` URI variants.\n\nThese changes reduce boilerplate in the extension host communication layer and ensure robust, unified path handling across the entire IPC surface, aligning with the project's Effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "8947f2ad49a775a37a130c6de9b1e11c132d486f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T11:02:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for URI sanitization and macro enhancement\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from 05ecea8 to 31f4058 to further standardize the Mountain native backend IPC layer.\n\n**Mountain:** Extend the `call!` macro in `WindServiceHandlers` with a new overload for handlers accepting no arguments, eliminating boilerplate across Extensions, Decorations, WorkingCopy, Keybinding, and Lifecycle dispatchers. Centralize URI sanitization by extracting `StripFileUriScheme` logic from `FileReadAlias.rs` into `Utilities::Params` as `strip_file_uri`, unifying the handling of `file://`, `file:///`, and `file://localhost` forms across the request tracking layer.\n\nThese changes reduce code duplication in the IPC dispatcher and ensure consistent path normalization for file system operations, aligning with the project's Effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "8c989b45611ebea4af8bf3cc158e78b2e79a9ed9"
		}
	],
